body:
Theme CSS media references: a theme's `theme.css` — and any CSS it `@import`s from within that same theme directory — may reference a file in the resolved library's shared `media/` tree using the reserved `media:` URL prefix, e.g. `url('media:fonts/EYInterstate-Regular.woff2')`. This lets several themes share one set of brand assets (fonts, backgrounds, logos) from a single library `media/` copy instead of duplicating the files and their `@font-face` CSS into every `themes/<name>/` directory or moving the styling into layouts. The path after the prefix is relative to the resolved library's `media/` (the SAME base as the layout `media` helper): it must not be absolute and must not contain `..` segments, and the file must exist — validated at load time (templates-dir-validation step 6) exactly like a layout `{{ media "path" }}` argument, with the error naming the theme CSS file and line. At serve time kalide rewrites every `media:` reference in the served theme CSS (theme.css and any CSS imported from the theme directory) to the served media URL — the same URL the layout `media` helper returns, so the browser fetches it from the resolved library's `media/`. The prefix is reserved: any other scheme in a theme CSS `url()` (`http:`, `https:`, `data:`, `//`, …), an absolute path, and a `..` escape all stay rejected (global.constraint.template-library-shareable). A theme may therefore reference only its own theme directory and the resolved library's `media/` tree — never another theme's directory and nothing outside the library. Both embedded authoring guides document the syntax (agent-authoring, library-agent-guide, agent-guide-drift-check).

AC:
- a `media:` reference in `theme.css` (and in a CSS it `@import`s from its own theme directory) to an existing file under the resolved library's `media/` loads cleanly, and the SERVED theme CSS exposes that file's served media URL, which resolves in the rendered deck (one copy of the asset, shared by every theme that references it);
- a `media:` reference to a missing file, to an absolute path (`media:/abs`), or to a path containing a `..` segment is a templates error naming the theme CSS file and line;
- a theme cannot reach another theme's directory or any path outside its own theme dir plus the library `media/` tree;
- both embedded guides document the reserved `media:` prefix, and removing that token from BOTH guides fails the agent-guide drift self-test (agent-guide-drift-check).
